<title>USA: Charter One says approval given for mergers.</title>
<headline>Charter One says approval given for mergers.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Charter One Financial Inc said Tuesday that the Office of Thrift Supervision (OTS) granted approval of the proposed merger between its subsidiary, Charter Michigan Bancorp and Haverfield Corp.</p>
<p>The company said the OTS also approved the merger of the companies' banking subsidiaries, Home Bank F.S.B and Charter One Bank F.S.B.</p>
<p>In a statement, Charter One Financial said Home Bank currently has $346 million in assets while its Charter One Bank has approximately $14.6 billion in total assets.</p>
<p>The deals are expected to close in the current quarter, pending Haverfield shareholder approval.</p>
</text>
